WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:12.660
I can't get into a love song

2
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:18.150
That's sung for a million people

3
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:24.740
This town critically tells me 
to love someone, but it's just

4
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.410
Easy love! Easy come! Easy go!

5
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:34.200
The future is much more 
realistic than I imagined

6
00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.910
It looks like cars won't 
be flying for a while

7
00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:45.060
And once again today, I'm on the subway

8
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:50.500
Left behind by the silent 
strangers and the town...

9
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:56.460
So I'm lonely lonely  Even on nights 
so lonely we're about to break

10
00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.850
Lonely lonely  It's only you who 
stays true to their original love

11
00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:07.320
Lonely lonely  Every day when 
I'm freezing and missing you

12
00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:13.060
I've decided not to force 
myself to say what I can't say

13
00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:18.250
That person is the only one 
who can make my heart hot

14
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:21.020
I wish I could forget...

15
00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.560
Love me Love Me  
This heart is strong yet weak

16
00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.530
Kiss me Kiss me  On nights 
when I'm alone and desperate

17
00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.430
Nobody knows what means love so

18
00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:37.770
Do you know how love song goes on?

19
00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:52.780
All the street racers respected her.
She was like a queen.

20
00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.660
In the wild "Last Signal" race,
where traffic lights went ignored...

21
00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:57.710
...she never lost,
and her fame became legendary...

22
00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:58.620
...as the "Queen of Hakosuka."

23
00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:02.540
That's Nao Kadena.
No doubt about it.

24
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.870
Queen of Hakosuka.

25
00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.040
The 30 million yen
which was promised...

26
00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:16.430
...I have deposited
in your account.

27
00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:20.350
So is the preparation
for the operation proceeding?

28
00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.980
School Infirmary

29
00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.770
Yes, as soon as the schedule
for the operation is set...

30
00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.540
...I'm going to tell my brother
about this.

31
00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:30.150
I'll wait for your call.
Thank you.

32
00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:45.410
Kichijoji Station

33
00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.910
This is what I bought
from Ms. Kadena.

34
00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.340
It's the technologically-advanced
"Miracle scope"...

35
00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.310
...developed by NASA
to search for planets.

36
00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:04.400
It's supposed to see
through any material.

37
00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.020
So if I use this,

38
00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:10.350
this becomes this...

39
00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.540
...then this...

40
00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:17.950
Our technology
sure has advanced with time.

41
00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:20.820
This is for me to keep up
with the new technology.

42
00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:22.960
switch... On!

43
00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:25.770
What? This way?

44
00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.880
What's this?
Strange!

45
00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.610
I can't see through anything.

46
00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.730
This cost me 200,000 yen!
What's going on?!

47
00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:35.550
Return my money!

48
00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:37.390
Return my money!

49
00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.920
What's this?
Weird.

50
00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:47.070
What did you say?
No returns?

51
00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.650
Don't joke with me.

52
00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:52.200
It isn't reasonable that the damaged
merchandise cost 200,000 yen.

53
00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.780
What does this mean,
Ms. Kadena?

54
00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:57.930
To call it damaged merchandise
is a false allegation.

55
00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:59.540
But you...

56
00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:02.570
Oh, don't tell me you had
a nasty plan...

57
00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:08.310
...to see under women's
clothes with this device.

58
00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.280
Why would I think like that?

59
00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:16.350
That's what I thought.

60
00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.410
There is no way that Vice Principal,
the model educator...

61
00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:22.760
...would have a dirty thought like that.

62
00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:26.320
I didn't say you could do it, either.

63
00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:30.270
Wait a minute, Ms. Kadena.

64
00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:31.900
Anything else?

65
00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:37.980
I'm hearing rumors about you.
You seem to have many problems.

66
00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:42.220
You gather students in the infirmary,
students who are skipping classes.

67
00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:44.830
You work as a hostess at night.

68
00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:48.290
Don't you know the school
prohibits our teachers...

69
00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.220
...from having another job?

70
00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:56.100
I'm going to report this
to the Chairman. Be prepared!

71
00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.190
Do whatever you like.

72
00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.010
Do whatever I like?

73
00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.180
What's with that attitude?!

74
00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:07.070
All of those young teachers...!
Like trash teacher, Onizuka...!

75
00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.890
It's strange.
I can't see through it.

76
00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:15.050
Mr. Onizuka?

77
00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.390
Oh, that is...!

78
00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:21.380
Ms. Fuyutsuki!
What's up?!

79
00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.660
Nice weather, isn't it?

80
00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.650
Mr. Onizuka!

81
00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:28.140
Mr. Onizuka, bad news!

82
00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.090
The Vice Principal wants
to fire Nao-chan.

83
00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:33.600
Leave him alone.

84
00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.560
He always tells me that.
But nothing happens.

85
00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.620
It's different in this case.

86
00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:40.270
Do you know anything,
Ms. Fuyutsuki?

87
00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.440
I'm not sure...

88
00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.910
- Let's go and see.
- Yeah.

89
00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:48.840
School Infirmary

90
00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.840
Are you sure you want
to quit school?

91
00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:53.300
What can I do?
The Vice Principal seems serious.

92
00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.990
He'll talk to the Chairman.

93
00:05:55.990 --> 00:05:59.190
Anyway,
I have enough money now.

94
00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:02.700
I knew this would happen
sooner or later, so I'm prepared.

95
00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:02.260
Resignation

96
00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:08.290
We'll do whatever we can.
You don't need to quit!

97
00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:11.880
That's right.
We're getting along well now.

98
00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:16.670
Thank you!
I'll be your friend always.

99
00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.240
But...

100
00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:21.020
Murai. I don't think
you can change her mind.

101
00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:25.540
This was her plan all along.

102
00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.650
She would quit school
right after she got enough money.

103
00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:31.080
Is it wrong?

104
00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.920
No. It's your choice.

105
00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:37.330
Don't quit, Nao-chan.

106
00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:41.590
Well, it sounds bad because
you say "quitting" and "firing."

107
00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:46.130
Nao-chan has reached her goal,
and she's leaving this school.

108
00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.500
We can call it "graduation."

109
00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:54.170
Let's give her a nice farewell.
Right, Ms. Fuyutsuki?

110
00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:55.670
I don't know!

111
00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:59.410
What are you angry at?
Fuyutsuki?

112
00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:00.640
Ms. Fuyutsuki!

113
00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:06.740
Ms. Fuyutsuki,
do you think it's our fault?

114
00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:09.650
We are skipping classes
and staying in the infirmary.

115
00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:11.760
Not only that...

116
00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:15.780
But we weren't just
playing around in there.

117
00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:20.000
We were getting advice
about our homes and the future.

118
00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:24.470
Me, too. My mother is young,
and I don't know what will happen.

119
00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.990
Girls were also telling her things...

120
00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:28.540
...they couldn't talk about
with anyone else.

121
00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:30.930
Is that so?

122
00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:35.350
She doesn't look like it,
but Nao-chan has had a hard life.

123
00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.820
She needs money
for someone in her family...

124
00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:40.180
...who was injured in an accident.

125
00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:40.750
What?

126
00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:44.690
Nerima Daiichi Motors

127
00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:45.540
Don't you specialize
in motorcycles?

128
00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:49.980
In the future we would like
to expand to used cars.

129
00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:53.600
That's why I would like
to ask for your advice.

130
00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:53.600
Garage R Manager
Ryuji Danma

131
00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:57.170
Our business is gloomy, too.
I'll think about it.

132
00:07:57.430 --> 00:07:58.730
Thank you!

133
00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:01.270
I envy Eikichi.

134
00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:04.740
Teachers don't need to lower
themselves in order to make sales.

135
00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:06.080
Aren't you Mr. Danma?

136
00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:10.920
I'm Muto. I used to be head
of the Nerima Massacre Group.

137
00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:14.480
Remember? We challenged Shonan
and were beaten by Onibaku.

138
00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:17.190
That's you.
It's been a while.

139
00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:22.850
Takashi, this is Mr. Ryuji Danma,
a partner of the legendary Onibaku.

140
00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:27.630
Hello. I'm Takashi Kadena.
I've heard about you from Muto.

141
00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:28.800
Kadena?

142
00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:32.340
He was a street racer in Yokohama.

143
00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:36.710
But he was a mechanic,
and his sister was more famous.

144
00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:39.010
That's enough.

145
00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:42.360
He doesn't like to talk
about the past.

146
00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:45.420
But he was the best mechanic.

147
00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.630
Of course.

148
00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:50.000
A little praise
makes you too snobby.

149
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.150
Hey, are you...?

150
00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.890
- What?
- What's up, Mr. Danma?

151
00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:02.500
Mr. Onizuka, your cell phone...

152
00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:08.020
Mr. Onizuka is away
from his desk now.

153
00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:09.970
Oh, Danma...!

154
00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:13.170
What? Ms. Kadena's brother?

155
00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:17.550
Hey! Can't you get down?!

156
00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:21.420
You're not doing it right at all!

157
00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:24.340
Everyone needs
one-on-one lessons!

158
00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:28.380
Only the body is growing up...

159
00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:38.160
It really hit him...

160
00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:41.300
Good job, Soldier Anne.

161
00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:44.710
Wonderful!
Did you see it hit him?!

162
00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.640
The next one is ready!

163
00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:50.460
Onizuka...
He's disturbing my class again.

164
00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.980
I won't allow him to do it today!

165
00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:58.220
Terrestrial Defense Force

166
00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:55.590
Attention,
Terrestrial Defense Force!

167
00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:58.220
Destroy Pervert Monster
Hokuroder!

168
00:09:58.590 --> 00:09:59.750
Yes!

169
00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:04.080
There isn't any reason
for you to call me a pervert!

170
00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:07.490
Yeah! Go, go!

171
00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.850
We did it!

172
00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:18.970
Ms. Kadena...

173
00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:21.910
What's up, Fuyutsuki?

174
00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:28.780
I acted like I was better than you,
without really knowing you...

175
00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:32.750
Forget about it, join us instead!

176
00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:37.490
This is fun, Fuyutsuki.
It's pretty good.

177
00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:43.160
Nao-chan.
Our object is gone.

178
00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:49.540
We're just starting to have fun!
Hokuroda! You chicken!

179
00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.250
Nao-chan. You're aggressive!

180
00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:52.690
Hokuroda was crying.

181
00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:56.260
We still have this much!

182
00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:01.580
I wanted to stay at this fun school
a little bit longer.

183
00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:05.110
Well, it's too late, I guess.

184
00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:11.410
I'm surrounded
by beautiful women...

185
00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:12.950
...and having free Sukiyaki!

186
00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:17.390
I guess this is heaven!

187
00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:23.380
No one said it's free.

188
00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:29.910
We're having the best beef.
It would cost a lot, wouldn't it?

189
00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:37.110
Yes, Sukiyaki and the service fees.
The total will be 125,000 yen.

190
00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:41.430
Payday is coming up,
so Mr. Onizuka can pay.

191
00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.460
Then I want him to pay everything
when he gets paid.

192
00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:46.480
No way...!

193
00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:48.290
Just kidding.

194
00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:50.130
What a dirty trick!

195
00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:53.760
They've ganged up to put me down
behind my back.

196
00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:57.090
Let's have a party tonight.

197
00:11:57.090 --> 00:12:00.570
We'll celebrate my graduation
and save the 30 million yen!

198
00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:03.750
Thirty million yen?!
What's that for?

199
00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:07.650
A member of my family
was in an accident.

200
00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:09.840
I was told that it would
cost that much...

201
00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:12.110
...for the surgery in the U.S.

202
00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:16.200
There are many foreign objects
in his body.

203
00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:19.090
We don't know when those objects
will reach the heart.

204
00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.670
But I have already paid in full.

205
00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:24.370
Now I'm just waiting for a call
from the person...

206
00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:25.710
...who arranged all of this.

207
00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:30.000
It's been a long time.
It was three years ago.

208
00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:34.410
Good evening. News time.

209
00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:37.420
A con man is wanted by the police.

210
00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:40.640
He's told victims he can arrange
for famous doctors...

211
00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:45.410
Medical Agent Fraud

212
00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:45.410
...to perform operations abroad.

213
00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:51.120
He scammed quite a bit of money
from his victims and then ran off.

214
00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:48.880
The con man...

215
00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:51.120
Is this...? Ms. Kadena?

216
00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:53.120
What are you talking about?

217
00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.090
This can't be true. No way.

218
00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:01.090
TONIGHT'S DINNER
IS SUKIYAKI

219
00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:07.240
Street racer?
How did you know?

220
00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.950
Even Murai and the others
don't know that.

221
00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:15.430
Mr. Onizuka's friend
saw you back then.

222
00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:22.250
At that time,
racing was my life.

223
00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.490
I was called
the Queen of Hakosuka.

224
00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:26.950
I was famous among the group.

225
00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:30.300
But one day you caused
an accident and lost a race...

226
00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:31.840
...then left the group.

227
00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:33.660
You knew that, too.

228
00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:36.960
The unexpected loss by
the Queen of Hakosuka is...

229
00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:39.690
...still a mystery
among the group.

230
00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:47.910
I'm wondering if the driver
in your car wasn't you...

231
00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:49.610
...but someone else.

232
00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:54.210
Maybe it's the person who needs
that operation in the U.S.

233
00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:58.070
Takashi Kadena,
my little brother.

234
00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:01.940
Takashi liked being a mechanic
more than racing.

235
00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:06.460
He was driving my Hakosuka
without telling me...

236
00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:10.730
...and was challenged by someone
who thought I was the driver.

237
00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:15.480
He couldn't decline, and he raced
"Last Signal" for the first time.

238
00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:44.280
It's a miracle that he survived
and recovered.

239
00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.060
But there is still
a problem with his eyes.

240
00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:49.580
That's a major obstacle...

241
00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:51.930
...when it comes to being
a top-notch mechanic.

242
00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:56.300
So he disappeared from my life.

243
00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:00.530
I was just too caught up in being
called the Queen of Hakosuka.

244
00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:03.200
It is, after all, my fault...

245
00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:05.460
...for getting him involved,
and then taking his dream away.

246
00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:11.500
I heard that
he'd completely recover...

247
00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:13.640
...if he has surgery in the U.S.

248
00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:17.120
Since then I concentrated
on making money.

249
00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:21.940
But when I thought I finally
had enough, it ends like this.

250
00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.270
It's strange, isn't it?

251
00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:28.480
Sorry.
It's a gloomy story.

252
00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:31.040
Ms. Kadena...

253
00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:36.240
You and I had different opinions,
but it was fun. Thank you.

254
00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:38.710
What are you going to do now?

255
00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.000
Well, I don't have any money now.

256
00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.520
I feel like I just lost everything
that kept me going.

257
00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:48.650
I don't know what to do.

258
00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:56.030
Don't worry. I'll survive.
See you.

259
00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:58.700
Can you say that
you're really living your life?

260
00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:08.270
Leave your brother alone.
Live your life!

261
00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:14.510
You're all outsiders.
No one understands how I feel.

262
00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:21.450
I don't understand. I don't want
to understand how you feel.

263
00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:31.500
What are you doing?

264
00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:34.450
Let's get the thing back...

265
00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:37.070
...the one thing that's
more important to you than money.

266
00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:46.380
What are you thinking?
You brought us all the way here.

267
00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.050
Thank you for waiting.

268
00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:56.190
Hey, Ryuji.

269
00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:09.200
Your order, one Hakosuka.
Here it is.

270
00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:14.610
It's aged a bit. But its performance
should be as good as it used to be.

271
00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:15.540
I can guarantee it.

272
00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:20.270
Let's start the "Last Signal."

273
00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:22.080
What are you thinking?

274
00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:28.140
Rather than thinking about the past,
isn't it better to die doing this?

275
00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:30.290
You would feel better
if you went quickly.

276
00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:33.860
Or are you afraid,
Queen of Hakosuka?

277
00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:50.910
Let's start!

278
00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:56.110
This has nothing to do with me.
You really could die.

279
00:18:19.940 --> 00:18:21.700
That's the way!

280
00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:30.140
Can you say
you're living your life?

281
00:18:58.110 --> 00:18:58.600
Idiot...

282
00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:03.680
Stop!!

283
00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:13.080
Whew, it's a tie.

284
00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.300
When I was in Yokohama...

285
00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.560
...I heard rumors
about Onibaku in Shonan.

286
00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:19.760
You lived up to the rumor.

287
00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:21.730
You, too.

288
00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.600
You're both alive.

289
00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:37.510
Takashi...

290
00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:41.040
Your brother built that Hakosuka.

291
00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:43.980
He asked us to get you back...
the way you used to be.

292
00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:46.950
Sorry that I didn't contact you
for so long...

293
00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:49.820
...but I wanted to escape from you.

294
00:19:51.820 --> 00:19:54.130
I liked when you drove Hakosuka.

295
00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:58.120
I don't want to see you
wasting your life for me.

296
00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:00.000
That accident was my fault.

297
00:20:00.350 --> 00:20:01.500
Takashi...

298
00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:06.700
...you have an unpredictable
problem with your body.

299
00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:11.410
Don't worry. I'll make money
by myself and have an operation.

300
00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:13.180
You live your own life.

301
00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:18.270
I'm not giving up.

302
00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:20.770
I'm still chasing my dream.

303
00:20:21.330 --> 00:20:25.650
Someday, I'll be someone
you can be proud of.

304
00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:26.590
Definitely!

305
00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:31.480
I'm stupid.
Without knowing how you felt...

306
00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:33.770
...I thought I was carrying
the burden all by myself.

307
00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:35.060
Really stupid...

308
00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.340
Sis...

309
00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:45.820
What's going on, everyone?
Why are you hurrying?

310
00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:46.970
Nao-chan...

311
00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:49.760
Sounds like Nao-chan
doesn't need to leave the school...!

312
00:20:50.450 --> 00:20:51.410
Really?

313
00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:55.350
School Infirmary

314
00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:01.100
Vice Principal?!

315
00:21:01.100 --> 00:21:03.120
Good morning, everyone.

316
00:21:04.850 --> 00:21:06.020
Vice Principal.

317
00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:09.000
Is it true that Ms. Kadena
doesn't have to leave school?

318
00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.680
Well, there were many problems.

319
00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:14.560
I think we need
a passionate teacher...

320
00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:17.000
...like Ms. Kadena in our school.

321
00:21:17.470 --> 00:21:20.240
I've decided not to report it
to the Chairman.

322
00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:23.670
As I thought about it, education
comes from passion. Passion!

323
00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:34.730
Well, then, I'm leaving now...

324
00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:42.310
Resignation

325
00:21:58.340 --> 00:22:03.140
You can't love everyone

326
00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:06.380
It's only for the one you love

327
00:22:06.580 --> 00:22:10.480
No breaking your faith or doubting

328
00:22:10.650 --> 00:22:15.920
Don't you judge or hate?

329
00:22:16.830 --> 00:22:20.470
Just stay innocent

330
00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:24.740
Am I hurting anyone?

331
00:22:24.930 --> 00:22:32.870
My emotion quietly blazes Deep inside my eyes

332
00:22:33.070 --> 00:22:37.680
I am so happy that I found you

333
00:22:39.340 --> 00:22:42.950
In the infinity of eternal time

334
00:22:43.110 --> 00:22:47.190
What is there for me to do?

335
00:22:47.350 --> 00:22:51.160
It may be small now

336
00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:55.400
But the fire cannot go out

337
00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:59.230
A tear is about to drop

338
00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:03.500
Hold it back in your chest

339
00:23:03.700 --> 00:23:07.370
Live strong every moment

340
00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:13.680
Like a single drop of your tear

341
00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:34.120
Next Episode

342
00:23:27.370 --> 00:23:30.140
Okay, then. I'm going to eat
all their staff's lunches.

343
00:23:30.140 --> 00:23:32.370
I was hungry.

344
00:23:33.060 --> 00:23:35.050
Please eat with me!

345
00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:37.500
To make her popular,
we need commercials.

346
00:23:38.860 --> 00:23:40.360
Mellow melon!

347
00:23:41.530 --> 00:23:45.450
Although we're amateurs, we know
Toroko's charm better than you.

348
00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.450
Interesting. If you say so,
I want you to do it.

349
00:23:52.280 --> 00:23:55.190
I finally got Toroko some work!
Don't interfere.

350
00:23:55.760 --> 00:23:56.960
It's thick and hard.

351
00:23:56.960 --> 00:24:01.960
SEE YA NEXT TIME
